  "title": "Experiment Design",
  "body": " Experiment Design   This assignment is due at the beginning of class on Monday, September 14 . It is graded based on completeness according to the rubric available on Canvas. It is open notes and collaboration with your group members is encouraged.     A medical researcher hypothesizes that GLP-1 medications, which are designed to stabilize Insulin-Like Growth Factors (ILGFs) in diabetic patients, could be used to assist nondiabetic patients with weight loss. They have found 100 patients willing to participate in the study.     For each level of measurement (nominal, ordinal, interval, and ratio), list one measurement (relevant to the study) that could be recorded from the patients. Justify your answers.      Which observation strategy (cross-sectional, retrospective, or prospective) would be best-suited for this experiment? Why?      For each sampling method we have discussed (random, systematic, stratified, and cluster), design a sampling scheme that could be used to assign the treatment group.      Between all sampling schemes you designed above, which do you think would produce the least bias in the results? Why?     "
